# L §5.11 At a computed key: "a chain that returns to a (def, keys) still being evaluated is refused at that key
# (RUN-CYCLE)."  x[k] reads x at the key nxt[k] gives; nxt[a] = b and nxt[b] = a.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ks = [a, b]
input nxt[k in ks]: key ks

def x[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = x[nxt[k]]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  nxt[a] = b
  nxt[b] = a

ask q1: x[a] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: refused: RUN-CYCLE ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
